<div id="alg2.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{new}\leftarrow\mathcal{P}_{new}+P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{new}\leftarrow\mathcal{P}_{new}+P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l29.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.l29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}=(\mathcal{E}_{t},objective_{t},fitness)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}=(\mathcal{E}_{t},objective_{t},fitness)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in T</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l30.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}\leftarrow\textsc{SortPopulation}(\mathcal{P},\mathcal{P}_{new})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SortPopulation</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}\leftarrow\textsc{SortPopulation}(\mathcal{P},\mathcal{P}_{new})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l31.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Sort combined population and reserve the top <math id="alg2.l31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l32.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Search Space of Dynamic Systems</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A dynamic system in real-time decision-making (e.g., ride-hailing dispatching) is characterized by time-evolving states and sequential interdependent decisions. Unlike static OR problems (e.g., traveling salesman problem or bin packing), dynamic systems require continuous adaptation to changing environments, leading to exponentially growing search spaces. The problem at time <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> can be formulated as: <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{t}=\{\mathcal{V}_{t},\mathcal{P}_{t},\mathcal{C}_{t},\mathcal{D}_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{t}=\{\mathcal{V}_{t},\mathcal{P}_{t},\mathcal{C}_{t},\mathcal{D}_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the system state at time <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, is composed by the vehicle set <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (taxis with locations and status), the passenger set <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (pending passenger requests with pickup/dropoff locations in time windows), constraint set <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (environment constraints) and historical decision trajectories up to <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> - <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At each decision step <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the dispatcher selects an action <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the action space (e.g., assigning taxis to requests and visiting order of each taxi). The system transitions to a new state <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the action <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is governed by: <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{t+1}=f(\mathcal{S}_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{t+1}=f(\mathcal{S}_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The search space <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> for a dynamic system is the union of all possible state-action sequences over a finite horizon <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\overset{T}{\underset{t=0}{\bigcup}}\{(\mathcal{S}_{t},a_{t})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑇</mo></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\overset{T}{\underset{t=0}{\bigcup}}\{(\mathcal{S}_{t},a_{t})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The action space <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at each step grows combinatorially with the number of vehicles <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of passenger requests <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{P}_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{P}_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the assignment between passengers and taxis at each step, its space can be <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|^{|\mathcal{P}|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{V}|^{|\mathcal{P}|})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> requests assigned to each taxi, the number of valid sequences is <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}!</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math> taxis, we can have <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((\mathcal{K}!)^{|\mathcal{V}|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((\mathcal{K}!)^{|\mathcal{V}|})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> steps, the total search space grows as <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{O}((|\mathcal{V}|^{|\mathcal{P}|}\mathcal{K}!^{|\mathcal{V}|})^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><msup><mo>!</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((|\mathcal{V}|^{|\mathcal{P}|}\mathcal{K}!^{|\mathcal{V}|})^{T})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This results in an extremely larger search space compared to traditional one-time OR problems, making it hard for direct resolution by LLM. While LLM continues to evolve, and current limitations may not persist in future iterations, the complexity of the search space necessitates a hybrid approach that integrates traditional optimization methods with LLM in a hierarchical framework. Therefore, we partition the problem into two levels:</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">LLM-driven objective design in high-level assignment model</h5>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LLM acts as meta-optimizer, dynamically proposing adaptive objectives to guide decision-making. The generated adaptive objective functions <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{t}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{t}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> encoding high-level goals, with current states <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and historical information <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> as inputs:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_centering ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>min</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{min}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi_{t}^{h}=LLM(\mathcal{S}_{t},H_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi_{t}^{h}=LLM(\mathcal{S}_{t},H_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s.t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s.t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{v}y^{pv}=1,\quad y^{pv}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{v}y^{pv}=1,\quad y^{pv}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">On the one hand, the assignment layer’s variables <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{pv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{pv}</annotation></semantics></math> lack direct visibility into sequencing outcomes (e.g., waiting times, route efficiency), on the other hand, a handcrafted objective (e.g., "minimize assignment distance") is myopic, as it ignores downstream sequencing impacts. To address this limitation, the LLM dynamically generates adaptive objectives <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{t}^{LLM}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{t}^{LLM}</annotation></semantics></math>
that implicitly steer assignments toward configurations favorable for low-level sequencing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Low-level sequencing model</h5>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a fixed assignment plan, each taxi shall solve a routing problem to visit the assigned passenger one by one, aiming to minimize the total passenger waiting time:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_centering ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>min</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{min}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi_{t}^{l}(\mathcal{S}_{t},\tau_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi_{t}^{l}(\mathcal{S}_{t},\tau_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s.t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s.t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g(S_{t},\tau_{t},a^{l}_{t})\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g(S_{t},\tau_{t},a^{l}_{t})\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the temporal variables (e.g., taxi arrival time), <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}^{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is the low-level action, namely, routing variables.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Direct Modeling Approach</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The complete taxi decision-making problem is formulated as a mixed-logic problem, where the objective is to minimize the passenger waiting time, incorporating constraints such as initial car and passenger location/time assignment, task connectivity constraint, vehicle travel dynamics and passenger boarding dynamics. The network we considered is defined as a directed graph <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\{\mathcal{S},\mathcal{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\{\mathcal{S},\mathcal{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of pick-up/dropoff stops in the network, with any stop <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is the route path between any two stops. Multiple passengers (taxis) may share the same origins and/or destinations. we utilize the service point sets <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A1.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(p,O^{p})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(p,O^{p})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(v,S^{v})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(v,S^{v})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, for origins) and <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A1.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(p,D^{p})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(p,D^{p})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(v,E^{v})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(v,E^{v})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, for destinations) to distinguish individual tasks while preserving both passenger geographical information.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initial and final car location assignment</h5>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Every time when a new planning occurs, the scheduler needs to know the initial taxi location, whether it is in idle state or driving on the road at this moment, we assume the time left for this taxi to arrive to its next immediate stop shall be known in advance, as depicted in constraints (<a href="#A1.E3.1" title="In 3 ‣ Initial and final car location assignment ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3a</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E3.2" title="In 3 ‣ Initial and final car location assignment ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3b</span></a>), respectively. Also, the taxi shall finally go back to the sink location after serving all assigned passengers, as captured in constraint (<a href="#A1.E3.3" title="In 3 ‣ Initial and final car location assignment ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3c</span></a>).</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E3.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathcal{P}}x_{(v,S^{v}),i}^{v}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathcal{P}}x_{(v,S^{v}),i}^{v}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E3.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle AR_{(v,S_{v})}^{v}=\tilde{t}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle AR_{(v,S_{v})}^{v}=\tilde{t}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E3.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathcal{P}}x_{i,(v,E^{v})}^{v}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathcal{P}}x_{i,(v,E^{v})}^{v}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{ij}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{ij}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates whether pick-up <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> dropoff pair <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ij" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ij</annotation></semantics></math> is selected for taxi <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AR_{i}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AR_{i}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is the arrival time of car <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> for pick-up service <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Passenger assignment constraints</h5>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each passenger can at most board on one car, as illustrated in (<a href="#A1.E4" title="In Passenger assignment constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v}y^{pv}=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></munder><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v}y^{pv}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Also, whenever a taxi <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is assigned to serve passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, it will firstly reach stop <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> to pick up the passenger, and subsequently proceed towards stop <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> to deliver the passenger to its destination. Thus, the operating taxi <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> shall confirm the edge OD for the selected passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v}\geq y^{pv}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v}\geq y^{pv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Service connectivity constraints</h5>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Whenever a group of services, each service incorporates a pick-up point and a dropoff point, are assigned to the taxi, for any two services, the taxi must complete one service before starting the next. In other words, if passengers <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are both assigned to the same taxi <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, then either passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is served first or the passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is served first. This order is reflected as a conservation law of typical Vehicle routing problem in current problem formulation, as captured in constraint (<a href="#A1.E6" title="In Service connectivity constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E6.x1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.x1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall v\in V,\forall i\in\mathcal{P},\forall j\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall v\in V,\forall i\in\mathcal{P},\forall j\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E6.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathcal{P}}x_{ij}^{v}=\sum_{q\in\mathcal{P}}x_{jq}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathcal{P}}x_{ij}^{v}=\sum_{q\in\mathcal{P}}x_{jq}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E6.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j\in\mathcal{D}}x_{ji}^{v}=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{D}}x_{ik}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j\in\mathcal{D}}x_{ji}^{v}=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{D}}x_{ik}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Also, each passenger must be served by one taxi, as illustrated in (<a href="#A1.E4" title="In Passenger assignment constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), accordingly, each pick-up or dropoff service point can only be visited one time by any of the taxi, as described below:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7.x1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.x1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall v\in V,\forall i\in\mathcal{P},\forall j\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall v\in V,\forall i\in\mathcal{P},\forall j\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{v}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{P}}x_{ij}^{v}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{v}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{P}}x_{ij}^{v}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{v}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{D}}x_{ij}^{v}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{v}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{D}}x_{ij}^{v}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Arrival and departure time constraints</h5>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If the route edge OD for passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is selected for taxi <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, then arrival time at dropoff point is equal to the sum of the pick up time at origin point and the OD travel time. Also, departure time at dropoff point is larger than its arrival time.</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8.x1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.x1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v}=1\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v}=1\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}=DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}+TR_{O^{p}D^{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}=DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}+TR_{O^{p}D^{p}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}\geq AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}\geq AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DP_{j}^{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DP_{j}^{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is departure time of car <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> for dropoff service <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\rightarrow B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\rightarrow B</annotation></semantics></math> is a logic constraint, indicating if <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is true, then implies <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Also, if passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is served immediately after passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> for taxi <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, then arrival time at pick-up point for passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the sum of the departure time of passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> at its dropoff point and the edge travel time. Also, departure time at pick-up point shall equal to the maximum value between the taxi arrival time and the passenger arrival/request time.</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E9.x1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.x1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}=1\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}=1\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E9.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}=DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}+TR_{D^{p}O^{p^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}=DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}+TR_{D^{p}O^{p^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E9.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle DP_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}=\text{max}(AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v},T^{p^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>max</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle DP_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}=\text{max}(AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v},T^{p^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Objective function</h5>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The goal is to minimize the total passenger waiting time, as captured below:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J=\sum_{p}\sum_{v}WT^{pv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>p</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J=\sum_{p}\sum_{v}WT^{pv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where waiting time <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="WT^{pv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">WT^{pv}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained from constraints below, only if passenger <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is assigned to taxi <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding waiting time <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="WT^{pv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">WT^{pv}</annotation></semantics></math> shall exist, otherwise, should be 0:</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E11.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y^{pv}=1\rightarrow WT^{pv}=DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-T^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y^{pv}=1\rightarrow WT^{pv}=DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-T^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E11.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y^{pv}=0\rightarrow WT^{pv}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y^{pv}=0\rightarrow WT^{pv}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">While alternative objectives, such as platform profit or driver earnings, can be incorporated to account for broader stakeholder impacts, this work does not aim to design a comprehensive or multi-faceted objective. Instead, it focuses on the interaction between the LLM and the optimizer, demonstrating how high-level goals specified via natural language can evolve into low-level objectives that guide decision-making. Extensions to other objectives are straightforward and left for future work.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed models above is formulated as a mixed logical model, incorporating both linear constraints and logical constraints (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In Arrival and departure time constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) (<a href="#A1.E9" title="In Arrival and departure time constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), and (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In Objective function ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). These logical constraints can be equivalently transformed into linear constraints using the big-M method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>, with detailed formulations provided in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS7" title="A.7 Logic Constraints Conversion ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>. Although the problem can be reformulated as a MILP model and solved directly using commercial solvers such as Gurobi to obtain optimal results, its large scale presents significant computational challenges. For instance, in a taxi-hailing system, each time can trigger a scenario with 80 taxis and 50 passenger requests, the decision variables <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{v}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{v}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> alone result in 200,000 (80*50*50) variables in MILP. Given the short decision-making intervals required in real-time operations, solving such a large-scale MILP optimally within the available time frame is impractical. Therefore, the problem is typically formulated as a sequential approach: first, solving an assignment problem to allocate a subset of passengers to a group of taxi drivers, followed by solving a traveling salesman problem with additional time constraints for each taxi independently in parallel.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Logic Constraints Conversion</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#A1.SS6" title="A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>, the problem has been formulated as a mixed logical dynamic model, which involves logic constraints, e.g.,arrival and departure time constraints (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In Arrival and departure time constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), (<a href="#A1.E9" title="In Arrival and departure time constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), and waiting time constraints (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In Objective function ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). All these logic constraints can be converted to linear constraints via big-M method as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Replacing logic constraints (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In Arrival and departure time constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) with Inequalities (<a href="#A1.E12" title="In A.7 Logic Constraints Conversion ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) in the model leads to the same solution.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span> Let <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be sufficiently large, and satisfies <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{1}\geq\underset{}{max}\{\pm(AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-TR_{(O^{p},D^{p})}),\pm(AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{1}\geq\underset{}{max}\{\pm(AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-TR_{(O^{p},D^{p})}),\pm(AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v})\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v\in V,p\in P\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V,p\in P\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then constraint (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In Arrival and departure time constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) can be rewritten as:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E12.x1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.x1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall v\in V,p\in P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall v\in V,p\in P</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E12.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-TR_{(O^{p},D^{p})}\leq M_{1}(1-x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-TR_{(O^{p},D^{p})}\leq M_{1}(1-x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E12.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}+DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}+TR_{(O^{p},D^{p})}\leq M_{1}(1-x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}+DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}+TR_{(O^{p},D^{p})}\leq M_{1}(1-x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E12.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}\leq M_{1}(1-x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}\leq M_{1}(1-x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12c)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E12.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}+DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}\leq M_{1}(1-x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-AR_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}+DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}\leq M_{1}(1-x_{(p,O^{p}),(p,D^{p})}^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12d)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Replacing logic constraints (<a href="#A1.E9" title="In Arrival and departure time constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) with Inequalities (<a href="#A1.E13" title="In A.7 Logic Constraints Conversion ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) in the model leads to the same solution.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span> Let <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be sufficiently large, and satisfies <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2}\geq\underset{}{max}\{\pm(AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-TR_{(D^{p},O^{p^{\prime}})}),AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-DP_{(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v},T^{p^{\prime}}-DP_{(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2}\geq\underset{}{max}\{\pm(AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-TR_{(D^{p},O^{p^{\prime}})}),AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-DP_{(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v},T^{p^{\prime}}-DP_{(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v\in V,p\in P\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V,p\in P\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then constraint (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In Arrival and departure time constraints ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) can be rewritten as:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E13.x1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.x1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall v\in V,p\in P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall v\in V,p\in P</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E13.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-TR_{(D^{p},O^{p^{\prime}})}\leq M_{2}(1-x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}-TR_{(D^{p},O^{p^{\prime}})}\leq M_{2}(1-x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E13.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}+DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}+TR_{(D^{p},O^{p^{\prime}})}\leq M_{2}(1-x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}+DP_{(p,D^{p})}^{v}+TR_{(D^{p},O^{p^{\prime}})}\leq M_{2}(1-x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E13.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle DP_{(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}\geq-M_{2}(1-x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle DP_{(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-AR_{(p^{\prime},O^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}\geq-M_{2}(1-x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13c)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E13.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle DP_{(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-T^{p^{\prime}}\geq-M_{2}(1-x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle DP_{(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v}-T^{p^{\prime}}\geq-M_{2}(1-x_{(p,E^{p}),(p^{\prime},D^{p^{\prime}})}^{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13d)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Replacing logic constraints (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In Objective function ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) with Inequalities (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.7 Logic Constraints Conversion ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) in the model leads to the same solution.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span> Let <math id="A1.SS7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> be sufficiently large, and satisfies <math id="A1.SS7.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{3}\geq\underset{}{max}\{\pm(WT^{pv}-DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-T^{p}),\pm(WT^{pv})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{3}\geq\underset{}{max}\{\pm(WT^{pv}-DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-T^{p}),\pm(WT^{pv})\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS7.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v\in V,p\in P\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V,p\in P\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then constraint (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In Objective function ‣ A.6 Direct Modeling Approach ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) can be rewritten as:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14.x1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.x1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall v\in V,p\in P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall v\in V,p\in P</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle WT^{pv}-DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-T^{p}\leq M_{3}(1-y^{pv})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle WT^{pv}-DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}-T^{p}\leq M_{3}(1-y^{pv})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-WT^{pv}+DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}+T^{p}\leq M_{3}(1-y^{pv})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>O</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-WT^{pv}+DP_{(p,O^{p})}^{v}+T^{p}\leq M_{3}(1-y^{pv})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle WT^{pv}\leq M_{3}y^{pv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle WT^{pv}\leq M_{3}y^{pv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14c)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle WT^{pv}\geq-M_{3}y^{pv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle WT^{pv}\geq-M_{3}y^{pv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14d)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>Dynamic Simulator Environment Setup</h3>

<div id="A1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the simulator, the state of the traffic network at time instant <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is simplified as <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(k)=\{d_{i}(k),t^{\text{arr}}_{i}(k),i\in\mathcal{I}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>arr</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(k)=\{d_{i}(k),t^{\text{arr}}_{i}(k),i\in\mathcal{I}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is the index of the taxi, <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of all taxis, <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is the location the <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th taxi at time instant <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is travelling to, and <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\text{arr}}_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>arr</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\text{arr}}_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is the time of the <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th taxi arriving that location. The following conventions are made for state and task update in the simulation:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1)</span>: the task being executed will not be reassigned.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2)</span>: if taxi has no task assigned, it will stay at destination of the last task.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The command issued from optimizer is a set of task sequences for each taxi in the traffic system. Each task has four parameters: origin <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, destination <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, passenger arrival time <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\text{start}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mtext>start</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\text{start}}</annotation></semantics></math>, taxi departure time <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\text{dep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mtext>dep</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\text{dep}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the command for the <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th taxi from the optimizer at time instant <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}^{opt}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}^{opt}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and the command being executed as <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. When the command from optimizer is issued to taxis, the command <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> will be set as <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}^{opt}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}^{opt}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. The command <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(k)=\{\text{task}_{i,0}(k),\ldots,\text{task}_{i,N_{i}}(k)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>task</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>task</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(k)=\{\text{task}_{i,0}(k),\ldots,\text{task}_{i,N_{i}}(k)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{task}_{i,j}(k)=(o_{i,j}(k),d_{i,j}(k),t^{\text{arr}}_{i,j}(k),t^{\text{start}}_{i,j}(k),t^{\text{dep}}_{i,j}(k))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>task</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>arr</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>start</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>dep</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{task}_{i,j}(k)=(o_{i,j}(k),d_{i,j}(k),t^{\text{arr}}_{i,j}(k),t^{\text{start}}_{i,j}(k),t^{\text{dep}}_{i,j}(k))</annotation></semantics></math> collecting origin, destination, taxi arrival time, passenger arrival time and taxi departure time from task origin, respectively. With system state <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and command <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u(k)=\{u_{i}(k),i\in\mathcal{I)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(k)=\{u_{i}(k),i\in\mathcal{I)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the state is updated as <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(k+1)=f(y(k),u(k),k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(k+1)=f(y(k),u(k),k)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is given as in Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ A.8 Dynamic Simulator Environment Setup ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for each <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.
When receiving new computed <math id="A1.SS8.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{opt}(k)=\{u_{i}^{opt}(k),i\in\mathcal{I}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{opt}(k)=\{u_{i}^{opt}(k),i\in\mathcal{I}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the state and command shall be updated as in <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ A.8 Dynamic Simulator Environment Setup ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> State Transition Model</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input</span>: Current state <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, commands <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(k)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output</span>: Next state <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow k+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each taxi <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(k)\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(k)\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(o_{c},d_{c},t^{\text{arr}}_{c},t^{\text{start}}_{c},t^{\text{dep}}_{c})\leftarrow\text{head}(u_{i}(k))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi><mtext>arr</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi><mtext>start</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi><mtext>dep</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>head</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(o_{c},d_{c},t^{\text{arr}}_{c},t^{\text{start}}_{c},t^{\text{dep}}_{c})\leftarrow\text{head}(u_{i}(k))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=t^{\text{arr}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>arr</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=t^{\text{arr}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
                 <span id="alg3.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}=o_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}=o_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
                  Update destination: <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\leftarrow d_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\leftarrow d_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
                  Update arrival time: <math id="alg3.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\text{arr}}_{i}\leftarrow t^{\text{dep}}_{c}+TR_{o_{c},d_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>arr</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi><mtext>dep</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\text{arr}}_{i}\leftarrow t^{\text{dep}}_{c}+TR_{o_{c},d_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
                 <span id="alg3.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
                  <math id="alg3.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{pop}(u_{i}(k))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>pop</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{pop}(u_{i}(k))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
                  <span id="alg3.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(k)\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(k)\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
                    <math id="alg3.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(o_{c},d_{c},t^{\text{arr}}_{c},t^{\text{start}}_{c},t^{\text{dep}}_{c})\leftarrow\text{head}(u_{i}(k))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi><mtext>arr</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi><mtext>start</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi><mtext>dep</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>head</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(o_{c},d_{c},t^{\text{arr}}_{c},t^{\text{start}}_{c},t^{\text{dep}}_{c})\leftarrow\text{head}(u_{i}(k))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
                    Move to next task: <math id="alg3.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\text{arr}}_{i}\leftarrow\max\{k,t^{\text{start}}_{c}\}+TR_{d_{i},o_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>arr</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi><mtext>start</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\text{arr}}_{i}\leftarrow\max\{k,t^{\text{start}}_{c}\}+TR_{d_{i},o_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\leftarrow o_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\leftarrow o_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
                  <span id="alg3.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
                 <span id="alg3.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
               Mark taxi <math id="alg3.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> as idle

</div>
<div id="alg3.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l21.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span> Command Update Protocol</figcaption>
<div id="alg4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg4.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input</span>: Optimized commands <math id="alg4.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\text{opt}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\text{opt}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, current state <math id="alg4.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(k)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output</span>: Updated commands <math id="alg4.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each taxi <math id="alg4.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg4.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg4.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(k)=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(k)=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg4.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(k+1)\leftarrow u^{\text{opt}}_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(k+1)\leftarrow u^{\text{opt}}_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg4.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
               Merge commands: <math id="alg4.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(k+1)\leftarrow\text{append}(u_{i}(k),u^{\text{opt}}_{i}(k))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>append</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(k+1)\leftarrow\text{append}(u_{i}(k),u^{\text{opt}}_{i}(k))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg4.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.9 </span>Prompt Engineering</h3>

<div id="A1.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the details of prompt strategies used in our method.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.9.1 </span>Scenario prompt compositions</h4>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ A.9.1 Scenario prompt compositions ‣ A.9 Prompt Engineering ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> illustrates the scenario prompt structure introduced in section <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS1" title="3.2.1 Scenario prompt setup ‣ 3.2 LLM-Optimizer Interaction Protocol ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.1</span></a>, where the scenario prompt is composed by <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\text{sys}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>sys</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\text{sys}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\text{geo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>geo</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\text{geo}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F15" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.10644v1/fig/ScenarioSetup.png" id="A1.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/348;" width="548" height="348" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F15.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 15</span>: </span><span id="A1.F15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Scenario prompt structure provided to LLM, including system architecture and role defintion (left panel), geospatical content (upper right panel), first-layer model blueprint (lower right panel)</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">System architecture <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> role definition (<math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\text{sys}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>sys</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\text{sys}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The system architecture and role definition establish the LLM as an adaptive objective designer rather than an end-to-end solver.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">System Architecture</span>: We provide a brief overview of the system architecture, including the communication between the simulator and the dispatcher, the two-level decomposition of the dispatching problem, namely,
<math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{assign}}:\min_{y}\mathcal{L}_{\text{assign}}(y|\theta_{\text{LLM}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>assign</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>assign</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>LLM</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{assign}}:\min_{y}\mathcal{L}_{\text{assign}}(y|\theta_{\text{LLM}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{route}}:\min_{x}\mathcal{L}_{\text{route}}(x|y^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>route</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>route</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{route}}:\min_{x}\mathcal{L}_{\text{route}}(x|y^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Role Specification</span>: Define the LLM’s role to constrain its outputs to objective function components compatible with the Gurobi <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> solver API using template-based generation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Geospatial context <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\text{geo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>geo</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\text{geo}}</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As the problem is related to ride-hailing services, incorporating geospatial context is essential. Therefore, we provide the testing environment details to the LLM. Utilizing the publicly available New York or Chicago taxi dataset, our analysis focuses on 19 zones in either Downtown Manhattan or extended Central Chicago. Static map data is represented as an OD matrix <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{OD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{OD}</annotation></semantics></math>, encoding spatial semantics via the Manhattan zone graph <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{E},W_{OD})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(\mathcal{V},\mathcal{E},W_{OD})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{OD}}[i,j]=t_{ij}\in\mathbb{R}^{+},\quad\forall(v_{i},v_{j})\in\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>OD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{OD}}[i,j]=t_{ij}\in\mathbb{R}^{+},\quad\forall(v_{i},v_{j})\in\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">First-layer model blueprint <math id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The first-level assignment model class structure is exposed to guide LLM-compatible objective design. This class structure provides a framework for the LLM to work within, ensuring that its output is consistent with the overall model design. By having access to the class structure, the LLM can understand the relationships between different variables and design an objective function that takes these relationships into account.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.9.2 </span>Harmony search prompt instruction</h4>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in section <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 Evolutionary prompt optimization ‣ 3.2 LLM-Optimizer Interaction Protocol ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a>, our evolutionary operators employ structured instruction blocks to guide LLM-based prompt optimization.
Specific instructions are listed as follows:</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Heuristic Improvement (<math id="A1.SS9.SSS2.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) Instruction Block:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Focuses on incremental objective refinement:</p>
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Temporal alignment: Incorporate taxi-passenger arrival time coordination.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Resource weighting: Adaptive taxi utilization coefficients</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Structural preservation: Maintain 50% legacy objective components.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Innovative Generation (<math id="A1.SS9.SSS2.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>) Instruction Block:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Promotes paradigm-level innovations:</p>
<ol id="A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Emphasis on goals: design first-level decisions <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{v,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{v,p}</annotation></semantics></math> minimize <span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">expected</span> second-level waiting:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\min\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}}\mathbb{E}\left[\max\left(DP_{p}^{(\text{2nd})}-t_{p}^{\text{arr}},0\right)\big|y_{v,p}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></munder><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>D</mi><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>2nd</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>p</mi><mtext>arr</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}}\mathbb{E}\left[\max\left(DP_{p}^{(\text{2nd})}-t_{p}^{\text{arr}},0\right)\big|y_{v,p}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multi-horizon optimization: Joint current/future state consideration</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Dynamic weight adaptation: Time-varying priority coefficients</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.9.3 </span>Gurobi format restriction</h4>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure the objective function is compatible with Gurobi, additional constraints are introduced to enhance its feasibility. Two types of restrictions are imposed:
1. <span id="A1.SS9.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Admissible Terms</span>: These constraints define the complete structure of the objective function, ensuring all components in the function adhere to the class requirements.
2. <span id="A1.SS9.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Expression Construction Rules</span>: Guidelines specifying the valid operations and transformations permitted in Gurobi’s expression framework to maintain solver compatibility.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Admissible components</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The generated objective functions must utilize only the following class elements, which are also summarized in Table <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Admissible components ‣ A.9.3 Gurobi format restriction ‣ A.9 Prompt Engineering ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decision variables</span>:
Binary assignments: <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{self.y[v,p]}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">self.y[v,p]</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{self.y[v,p]}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Static parameters</span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Distance matrix: <span id="A1.I4.i2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">self.distMatrix[o][d]</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Big-M constant: <span id="A1.I4.i2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">self.M</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Taxi state</span> (read-only):</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I4.i3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Current position: <span id="A1.I4.i3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">self.taxi[v].start_pos</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I4.i3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Availability time: <span id="A1.I4.i3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">self.taxi[v].arrival_time</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Passenger state</span> (read-only):</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I4.i4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Origin/Destination: <span id="A1.I4.i4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">self.passenger[p].origin</span>, <span id="A1.I4.i4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">self.passenger[p].destination</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I4.i4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Request time: <span id="A1.I4.i4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">self.passenger[p].arrTime</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 7</span>: </span><span id="A1.T7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Model specification mapping</span></figcaption>
<table id="A1.T7.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T7.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T7.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T7.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Concept</span></th>
<th id="A1.T7.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T7.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Mathematical Form</span></th>
<th id="A1.T7.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T7.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Code Implementation</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T7.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T7.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Assignment variable</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{v,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{v,p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T7.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">self.y[v,p]</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T7.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Travel time matrix</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TR_{o,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TR_{o,d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T7.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">self.distMatrix</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T7.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Taxi availability</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{v}^{\text{avail}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">avail</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{v}^{\text{avail}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T7.5.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">self.taxi[v].arrival_time</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T7.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Passenger request time</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{p}^{\text{req}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">req</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{p}^{\text{req}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T7.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">self.passenger[p].arrTime</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A1.T7.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Weighted sum</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A1.T7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum w_{i}c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum w_{i}c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A1.T7.5.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">sum(w * c for w, c in zip(weights, costs))</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Expression construction rules</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All objectives must adhere to:</p>
<ol id="A1.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Structural requirements</span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Costs stored in list <span id="A1.I5.i1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">costs</span> (1-5 elements)</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Weights in list <span id="A1.I5.i1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">weights</span> (length matching <span id="A1.I5.i1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">costs</span>)</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Final objective: <span id="A1.I5.i1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sum(w*c for w,c in zip(weights, costs)</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gurobi expression rules</span>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I5.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Use <span id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">**gb.quicksum()/gb.max_()/gb.abs_()**</span> only when containing variables</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Use <span id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">**sum()/max()/abs()**</span> when working with parameters</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Quadratic terms via variable multiplication (<span id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">y[v,p]*y[v,q]</span>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Never multiply Gurobi variables with Gurobi expressions 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"> - Invalid: y[v,p] * gb.max_(expression_with_vars, 0)</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Never use Python if/else with Gurobi variables/expressions</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generation protocol</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following template is provided to LLM for valid objective construction:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para"><pre id="A1.SS9.SSS3.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
def dynamic_obj_func(self):
    cost1 = [Proper Gurobi expression]
    cost2 = [Proper Gurobi expression]
    # Add more components as needed

    # Custom weights (match costs length)
    weights = [
        [Your custom weight 1],
        [Your custom weight 2],
        # Add matching weights
            ]
    objective = sum(w*c for w,c in zip(weights, costs))
    self.model.setObjective(objective, gb.GRB.MINIMIZE)
</pre>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.9.4 </span>LLM response examples</h4>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ Sequential assignment with dropoff-pickup chaining ‣ A.9.4 LLM response examples ‣ A.9 Prompt Engineering ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A1.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ Sequential assignment with dropoff-pickup chaining ‣ A.9.4 LLM response examples ‣ A.9 Prompt Engineering ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> illustrate four LLM response examples generated by the proposed method. The first-layer model blueprint defines the default objective function, serving as a foundational heuristic for the LLM, as captured in Figure <a href="#A1.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ A.9.4 LLM response examples ‣ A.9 Prompt Engineering ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>. The listed four objective function variants capture different optimization strategies:</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F16" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.10644v1/fig/defaultObj.png" id="A1.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:499/84;" width="499" height="84" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F16.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 16</span>: </span><span id="A1.F16.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Default objective code used in first-layer model blueprint</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Weighted multi-objective with dynamic penalties</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As captured in left panel of Figure <a href="#A1.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ Sequential assignment with dropoff-pickup chaining ‣ A.9.4 LLM response examples ‣ A.9 Prompt Engineering ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, unlike the static weights in the default, this variant introduces dynamic penalties (e.g., time-scaled idle taxi prioritization in <math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, future availability adjustments in <math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>) and amplifies priority weights (e.g., 80 for waiting time, 1000 for load imbalance). By dynamically scaling penalties based on real-time conditions (e.g., taxi arrival vs. passenger request times), it adaptively balances short-term efficiency and long-term fleet availability, addressing the default’s rigidity in handling time-dependent scenarios.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Quadratic load balancing with reassignment penalty</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While the default penalizes load imbalance via <math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, this variant (shown in right panel Figure <a href="#A1.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ Sequential assignment with dropoff-pickup chaining ‣ A.9.4 LLM response examples ‣ A.9 Prompt Engineering ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) explicitly enforces fairness through a squared deviation from the average passenger-per-taxi ratio (load_balance). Furthermore, this variant incorporates a quadratic reassignment penalty (<math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>) to minimize frequent taxi reassignments. This dual focus effectively reduces reassignment churn and strengthens fairness, addressing the limitations of the default model in enforcing balanced allocations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Busy taxi penalty with load balancing</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Replacing the default’s simplistic waiting time penalty, this variant (captured in left panel of Figure <a href="#A1.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ Sequential assignment with dropoff-pickup chaining ‣ A.9.4 LLM response examples ‣ A.9 Prompt Engineering ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) directly penalizes assignments to busy taxis using a <math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> operator (<math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>) to check if a taxi’s availability precedes the passenger’s request. This variant incorporates the full trip duration into <math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, extending beyond the default model’s focus on pickup times alone. Additionally, it maintains quadratic load balancing to distribute demand more effectively. By considering both real-time availability and total trip effort, this approach prevents excessive assignments to already occupied taxis, addressing a key limitation of the default model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sequential assignment with dropoff-pickup chaining</h5>

<div id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike the default’s isolated trip modeling, this variant (captured in right panel of Figure <a href="#A1.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ Sequential assignment with dropoff-pickup chaining ‣ A.9.4 LLM response examples ‣ A.9 Prompt Engineering ‣ Appendix A Technical Appendices ‣ Hierarchical Optimization via LLM-Guided Objective Evolution for Mobility-on-Demand Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) introduces a sequential chaining mechanism in <math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, penalizing dropoff-to-pickup travel time between passengers (<math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y[v,p]*y[v,p\_]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y[v,p]*y[v,p\_]</annotation></semantics></math>). It also adds bidirectional waiting time penalties (<math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for taxi delay, <math id="A1.SS9.SSS4.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cost_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cost_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> for passenger earliness), whereas the default only penalizes taxi delays. By optimizing trip sequences and accounting for both waiting constraints, it enhances fleet utilization efficiency, which is an improvement over the default’s single-trip optimization approach.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F17" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.10644v1/fig/promptResponse1.png" id="A1.F17.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/353;" width="548" height="353" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F17.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 17</span>: </span><span id="A1.F17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">LLM response examples, including dynamic penalty variant (left panel) and quadratic loading balancing variant (right panel)</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F18" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.10644v1/fig/promptResponse2.png" id="A1.F18.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/367;" width="548" height="367" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F18.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 18</span>: </span><span id="A1.F18.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">LLM response examples, including busy taxi variant (left panel) and sequential assignment variant (right panel)</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
